The Lean installation itself is intact; the audit container’s PID namespace makes Lean’s `/proc/<pid>/exe` lookup fail because `/proc` exposes a different namespace. I confirmed the cause at the system-call path and applied a narrow read-only lookup shim that maps only `/proc/<pid>/exe` to `/proc/self/exe`. With the pinned Lean 4.22.0 toolchain, the generated project now clean-builds; I’m rerunning the unchanged trusted preflight under that environment and recording both the initial failures and the corrected run.
